        <mxCell id="card_dev_oidc" value="GitHub OIDC Role&#10;dev-apply (ADR-003)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3410" y="795" width="140" height="48" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="badge_d06_doidc" value="D06" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0284c7;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3535" y="785" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dev_text" value="Development Account Components:&#10;• Sandbox Environment: dev account for experimental development and testing.&#10;• Dev VPC (10.80.0.0/16) [D04] with development subnet layout.&#10;• S3 State Bucket (aroma-dev-tfstate) [D02] with native object locking.&#10;• GitHub OIDC Federation [D06]: dev-plan and dev-apply IAM roles.&#10;• Dev Instances: Lightweight developer resources, mocks, and sandboxes.&#10;• Audit Logs: Local CloudWatch log group (operational only);&#10;  records are NOT archived to Security account (ASM-068).&#10;• Boundary Rule: Isolated from QA and Production; holds NO production data." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3095" y="860" width="675" height="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="panel_identity" value="IDENTITY ENTRY POINTS (Exactly 4 Kinds | Section 4 &amp; docs/security-and-identity.md Section 4)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#334155;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1255" width="1140" height="770" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="id_k1" value="1. AWS Human Operators (Platform Operator, Auditor, Break-Glass) [D06]&#10;• Entry Point: IAM Identity Center (Organization instance in Management Account; delegated admin in Security Account).&#10;• Authentication: Mandatory Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) via TOTP software token on smartphone.&#10;• Access Control: One permission set per role, assigned per account; ZERO long-term IAM users or static keys.&#10;• Role Mapping:&#10;  - Auditor: Read-only access to Audit Archive bucket and Athena query workspace in Security Account.&#10;  - Platform Operator: Operations access to application log groups and AWSIotLogsV2 in workload accounts.&#10;  - Break-Glass: Emergency operational access, invoked only under recorded incident reference (A09)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1295" width="1100" height="155" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="id_k2" value="2. CI / CD Pipeline Automation (GitHub Actions) [D06]&#10;• Entry Point: GitHub OIDC Identity Provider configured in each environment account (dev, qa, pdn).&#10;• Security: Cryptographic OIDC federation exchanging signed GitHub JWT for temporary AWS STS credentials.&#10;• Access Control: Per-environment plan and apply IAM roles (ADR-003). Strictly ZERO static credentials or stored AWS keys." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1465" width="1100" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="id_k3" value="3. Hardware Devices (Crop Nodes, Drying Nodes, and Drones) [D06]&#10;• Entry Point: AWS IoT Core Thing Registry in each workload account (dev, qa, pdn).&#10;• Authentication: Mutual TLS (mTLS) with unique X.509 client certificate registered from CSR (port 8883 / 443 ALPN).&#10;• Certificate Lifecycle: Immediate revocation by certificate status check. Drones obtain upload grants before flight delivery." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1590" width="1100" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="id_k4" value="4. Application Users (8 Business Roles | security-and-identity.md Section 4) [D06]&#10;• Entry Point: Amazon Cognito User Pools located in the workload account (pdn):&#10;  * Staff Pool (MFA required with TOTP):&#10;    - Collection-Center Operator, Drone Operator, Agronomist, Platform Operator.&#10;    - Sensitive operations (fumigation authorization, threshold change, cert revoke) require re-authentication if auth_time &gt; 10 min.&#10;  * Field Pool (No MFA, justified adoption decision ASM-091):&#10;    - Farmer, Transporter, Read-Only Buyer.&#10;    - Passwordless SMS code to registered phone; 30-day refresh token; hardware-backed keystore offline outbox encryption (ASM-095).&#10;  * Anonymous Public Reader:&#10;    - Public sack lookup by code only; unauthenticated, no Cognito user pool (ASM-069). Zero cédula or full trace returned." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1715" width="1100" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="panel_audit" value="AUDIT PIPELINE FOR THE FOUR MANDATORY EVENTS (Section 7 | 5-Year Retention under Object Lock)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#047857;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#064e3b;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1205" y="1255" width="1500" height="770" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="audit_ov" value="Dual-Layer Audit Architecture (Section 7):&#10;• Layer 1 (AWS CloudTrail): Authoritative for AWS API calls made by identifiable principals (S3 flight object uploads, pipeline apply).&#10;• Layer 2 (Application &amp; IoT Core): Authoritative for domain business events (sack reads, threshold changes, MQTT publications).&#10;• Compliance Retention: All audit records stored for 5 years in Security Account under S3 Object Lock compliance mode (ASM-067)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#10b981;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1225" y="1295" width="1460" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ev1_box" value="1. Sack Read Audit (Public Web, Farmer App, Center App)&#10;• Writing Layer: Application lookup service (CloudFront + WAF + Lambda URL).&#10;• Audit Record: Structured JSON written to /aws/application/audit in pdn.&#10;• Content: Authenticated user and role (buyer, farmer, center op) or &#x27;anonymous&#x27; (ASM-069);&#10;  sack code, view returned (buyer/center/farmer), result (found/not found/denied),&#10;  UTC timestamp, source IP, channel (web/farmer/center app), user agent.&#10;• Privacy Guard: NO national ID (cédula) and NO full trace recorded (Point 2 requirement).&#10;• Shipping Path: CloudWatch Subscription -&gt; Data Firehose -&gt; s3://audit-archive/application/" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#86efac;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#064e3b;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1225" y="1405" width="715" height="185" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ev2_box" value="2. Threshold Change Audit (Reports Web / Threshold Config)&#10;• Writing Layer: Application threshold service (written in same transaction).&#10;• Audit Record: Structured JSON written to /aws/application/audit in pdn.&#10;• Content: Federation agronomist or platform operator identity with MFA; variable,&#10;  zone (crop/drying), scope (pilot/farm), old value, new value, reason, UTC time, source IP.&#10;• Secondary Audit: CloudTrail write-only data events on thresholds DynamoDB table (PD-074).&#10;• Shipping Path: CloudWatch Subscription -&gt; Data Firehose -&gt; s3://audit-archive/application/" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#86efac;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#064e3b;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1970" y="1405" width="715" height="185" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ev3_box" value="3. Telemetry Publication Audit (Crop &amp; Drying MQTT Readings)&#10;• Writing Layer: AWS IoT Core.&#10;• Accepted Publications: Telemetry topic rule writes reading + metadata directly to&#10;  DynamoDB telemetry store: node ID, cert principal, client ID, source IP, receive time, original timestamp.&#10;• Rejected Publications: Authorization or TLS failures logged at ERROR level in AWSIotLogsV2 log group.&#10;• Retention: 5 years in DynamoDB telemetry store (case statement requirement for readings).&#10;• Ingress Path: Direct via cellular bearer to regional IoT Core endpoint (bypasses center &amp; VPC)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#86efac;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#064e3b;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1225" y="1605" width="715" height="175" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ev4_box" value="4. Flight Object Delivery Audit (Drone Mission Upload)&#10;• Writing Layer: AWS CloudTrail (S3 Data Events) and Reception Lambda Function.&#10;• Audit Record: CloudTrail S3 data events (PutObject, CompleteMultipartUpload) on pdn drone&#10;  bucket by ARN prefix. Captures principal, bucket, key, version, size, eventTime, source IP.&#10;• Flight Linking: Reception function links S3 object to flight record in transactional store (ADR-002).&#10;• Pilot Attribution: Upload-grant record binds pilot identity &amp; drone kit to upload authorization (PD-075).&#10;• Shipping Path: Multi-Region Organization Trail -&gt; s3://audit-archive/AWSLogs/&lt;org-id&gt;/" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#86efac;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#064e3b;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1970" y="1605" width="715" height="175" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="audit_stor" value="Centralized Audit Storage &amp; Verification (Security Account)&#10;• Target S3 Bucket: s3://aroma-audit-archive-shared (us-east-1)&#10;• Integrity &amp; Compliance: S3 Object Lock in COMPLIANCE MODE (5-year default retention, ASM-067). Cannot be shortened or deleted by any user or root.&#10;• Encryption: Customer-Managed KMS Key (audit key) under Security account policy. S3 Block Public Access, Versioning, TLS 1.2+ enforce.&#10;• Partitioning: s3://.../AWSLogs/&lt;org-id&gt;/ (CloudTrail org events) | s3://.../application/ (Firehose-streamed application audit logs)&#10;• Verification: Amazon Athena workspace configured for Auditor role to execute SQL queries across both audit streams." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#10b981;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1225" y="1800" width="1260" height="155" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="auditor_card" value="Auditor Role&#10;(IAM Identity Center)" style="shape=umlActor;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;html=1;outlineConnect=0;fillColor=#064e3b;strokeColor=#064e3b;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2540" y="1820" width="45" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="athena_badge" value="Athena SQL&#10;Workspace" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#8C4FFF;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2605" y="1835" width="95" height="45" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="edge_auditor_athena" value="Queries" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#059669;align=center;" edge="1" parent="1" source="athena_badge" target="audit_stor">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="edge_ev4_to_storage" value="CloudTrail Org Trail Stream -&gt; AWSLogs/&lt;org-id&gt;/" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;fontColor=#064e3b;align=center;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.8;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ev4_box" target="audit_stor">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="panel_budgets" value="BUDGETS &amp; COST ALERTING ARCHITECTURE (Section 6 | Management Account)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#b45309;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#78350f;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2730" y="1255" width="1110" height="770" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="budgets_ov_box" value="Centralized Cost Governance (Section 6):&#10;• All budgets created in Management Account over linked accounts; values follow A23 cost model (PD-076).&#10;• Historical note: 2020 prices are retired; no 2020 figure is used for budget baselines (legacy-2020.md).&#10;• Budgets split by cost allocation tags and linked accounts to mirror the 5 case dimensions." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2750" y="1295" width="1070" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="budgets_cat_box" value="AWS Budgets Catalog (11 Monthly Cost Budgets | Section 6)&#10;1. Farms Budget: Filter CostCenter = farms, pdn account. Ingestion, telemetry store, threshold function.&#10;2. Drones Budget: Filter CostCenter = drones, pdn account. Ingress, S3 flight objects, inference functions.&#10;3. Collection Centers Budget: Filter CostCenter = collection-centers, pdn; child budget per center.&#10;4. Trips Budget: Filter CostCenter = trips, pdn account. Transporter position ingestion and store.&#10;5. Testing Budget: Linked accounts test (qa) and development (dev), all cost (ASM-064).&#10;6. Account Budgets (6 budgets): One budget per linked account (mgmt, sec, net, pdn, qa, dev).&#10;&#10;Alert Threshold Triggers (ASM-066):&#10;• Actual 80 % (early warning) | Actual 100 % (budget reached) | Forecasted 100 % (month-end projection)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#fde68a;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#78350f;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2750" y="1405" width="1070" height="245" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="budgets_flow_box" value="Alert Path and Automated Budget Actions (Section 6)&#10;• Alert Notification Flow:&#10;  AWS Budgets + AWS Cost Anomaly Detection (2 monitors: linked account &amp; CostCenter tag)&#10;  --&gt; Amazon SNS Topic in Management Account (encrypted with customer-managed KMS key)&#10;  --&gt; Subscribers: Platform Operator role and designated Cost Owner (email / SMS).&#10;• Testing Budget Automated Action (Guardrail):&#10;  * Trigger: At actual 100% test spend on Testing Budget.&#10;  * Governance Gate: Requires MANUAL APPROVAL by Cost Owner / Lead.&#10;  * Action: Applies SCP to NonProduction OU denying creation of new AWS resources.&#10;• Production Protection Rule (RTO Guardrail):&#10;  * Production OU NEVER receives an automatic budget stop action.&#10;  * Preserves continuous farmer alert delivery and public sack lookup (4-hour RTO requirement)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2750" y="1665" width="1070" height="255" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
